# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# GREY PROJECT - ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES TEMPLATE
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for development or .env for production
# IMPORTANT: Never commit .env files with real secrets to Git
# Always set passwords and tokens through cPanel environment variables
#
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 1: ENVIRONMENT & SERVER
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Environment mode
# development   = Enable hot reload, verbose logging, debug tools
# production    = Optimized build, minimal logging, strict error handling
NODE_ENV=development

# Server port
# Development:  3000 (localhost)
# Production:   3000 (0.0.0.0 for cPanel) or use cPanel's assigned port
PORT=3000

# Server hostname
# Development:  localhost (local machine only)
# Production:   0.0.0.0 (accept requests from any IP - required for cPanel)
HOST=localhost


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 2: DATABASE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# SQLite database file location
# Development:  file:./Admin/data/grey.db (local file-based)
# Production:   file:./Admin/data/grey.db (same, cPanel will create the directory)
# 
# NOTE: SQLite auto-creates the file and directory on first access
# No need to manually create Admin/data/ directory
DATABASE_URL=file:./Admin/data/grey.db

# Optional: PostgreSQL (if you want to migrate from SQLite)
# Leave commented for SQLite. To enable:
# 1. Uncomment the line below
# 2. Update lib/db.ts to use PostgreSQL
# 3. Run migrations on your PostgreSQL server
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/grey_db


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 3: SECURITY - SESSIONS & CSRF PROTECTION
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Session secret for expressing session middleware
# IMPORTANT: Generate a new secure random string for production!
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# 
# If empty, a random secret is auto-generated on first run and saved to .secrets.json
# For production, explicitly set this to ensure consistency across server restarts
SESSION_SECRET=dev-session-secret-change-in-production

# CSRF protection secret (double-submit token verification)
# IMPORTANT: Generate a new secure random string for production!
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# If empty, a random secret is auto-generated on first run
CSRF_SECRET=dev-csrf-secret-change-in-production


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 4: STRIPE PAYMENT GATEWAY
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Stripe API Keys
# Test Keys (Development): Start with "pk_test_" and "sk_test_"
# Production Keys: Start with "pk_live_" and "sk_live_"
#
# Get keys from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
# Never commit live keys to Git
STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_YOUR_TEST_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_YOUR_TEST_SECRET_KEY_HERE

# Stripe webhook secret (for handling payment events)
# Get from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
# Only needed if your app listens to Stripe webhooks
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_test_YOUR_WEBHOOK_SECRET_HERE


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 5: PAYPAL PAYMENT GATEWAY
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# PayPal API Credentials
# Test Mode: Use sandbox credentials from https://developer.paypal.com
# Production: Use live credentials (keep very secret!)
#
# Never commit live credentials to Git
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=test_YOUR_TEST_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=test_YOUR_TEST_PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET

# PayPal mode: sandbox or live
# Set to "sandbox" for testing
# Set to "live" for production (with live credentials above)
PAYPAL_MODE=sandbox


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 6: EMAIL CONFIGURATION (SMTP)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# SMTP Server Details
# Option A: Gmail
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com
#   SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-specific-password (NOT your Gmail password!)
#   Get app-specific password from: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#
# Option B: SendGrid
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.sendgrid.net
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=apikey
#   SMTP_PASSWORD=SG.your-sendgrid-api-key
#
# Option C: Custom SMTP server
#   SMTP_HOST=mail.example.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=your-email
#   SMTP_PASSWORD=your-password

# Gmail example (change for your email provider):
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-email@greyinfotech.com.ng
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-specific-password

# From address for outgoing emails
SMTP_FROM=noreply@greyinfotech.com.ng

# Reply-to address
SMTP_REPLY_TO=support@greyinfotech.com.ng


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 7: AUTHENTICATION - SEED CREDENTIALS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Initial admin user passwords (used by `npm run seed`)
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES:
# - These are used to create initial admin accounts when database is empty
# - Change these IMMEDIATELY after first login to production
# - Store actual production passwords in cPanel environment variables
# - Never commit production passwords to Git
#
# Passwords must be at least 8 characters (bcrypt will hash them)
# Special characters recommended for security

# Super Admin (Full system access)
# Email: admin@greyinfotech.com.ng
SEED_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!ChangeMeInProduction

# Admin (Can manage most features)
# Email: admin@greyinfotech.com.ng
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@greyinfotech.com.ng
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!ChangeMeInProduction

# Project Manager
# Email: pm@greyinfotech.com.ng
SEED_MANAGER_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!ChangeMeInProduction

# Support Staff
# Email: support@greyinfotech.com.ng
SEED_STAFF_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!ChangeMeInProduction


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 8: API & PUBLIC URLs
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Public API base URL (used by frontend for API calls and email links)
# Development:  http://localhost:3000
# Production:   https://your-domain.com (must match your actual domain)
#
# IMPORTANT: Must be accessible publicly and use HTTPS in production
# Used in: Email links, JWT tokens, API client initialization
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: Admin API base URL (if different from main API)
# Leave empty to use NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/admin/api


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 9: LOGGING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Log level controls verbosity of server logs
# error   = Only errors
# warn    = Errors and warnings
# info    = Errors, warnings, and general info (RECOMMENDED)
# debug   = All of the above plus detailed debug info
# trace   = Extremely verbose (dev only)
LOG_LEVEL=info


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 10: RATE LIMITING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Rate limit window in milliseconds
# 900000ms = 15 minutes (recommended)
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=900000

# Maximum requests per window per IP
# 100 = 100 requests per 15 minutes (recommended for login endpoints)
# Adjust higher for APIs with legitimate bulk requests
RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=100


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 11: OPTIONAL - ADVANCED FEATURES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Redis Cache (Optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable (uses in-memory cache)
# To enable: Set Redis connection string
# Format: redis://[user][:password]@[host]:[port]/[db]
# Example: redis://default:password@localhost:6379/0
REDIS_URL=

# ─── Sentry Error Tracking (Optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable
# Get DSN from: https://sentry.io
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# ─── GitHub Integration (Optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable
# Get token from: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# Needed for: Code analysis features, GitHub integration
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ─── Analytics (Optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable
# Mixpanel token for analytics tracking
MIXPANEL_TOKEN=

# ─── Recaptcha (Optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable
# Get keys from: https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin
RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=

# ─── Google Maps API (Optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable
# Get key from: https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 12: cPanel-SPECIFIC SETTINGS (Production Only)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# These should be set in cPanel Node.js App Manager > Edit Variables
# Not in .env file (which cPanel might not read)

# Node.js version (cPanel shows in UI)
# Should be 18.x or higher
# Set in cPanel: Node.js App Manager > Node.js version dropdown

# Memory limit for npm install (cPanel has limited RAM)
# Set in .npmrc or via environment:
# NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=256"

# App startup file
# cPanel expects: server.js or app.js
# Ours is: server.ts (compiled by tsx)
# Set in cPanel: Application startup file = "server.js" or "npm start"


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# DEVELOPMENT SETUP:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env.local
# 2. Leave most defaults, just ensure DATABASE_URL is set
# 3. Run: npm run seed (creates demo admin users)
# 4. Run: npm run dev (starts server on localhost:3000)
#
# PRODUCTION SETUP (cPanel):
# 1. Clone code to cPanel via Git or FTP
# 2. Do NOT commit .env files to Git
# 3. In cPanel Node.js App Manager > Edit Variables:
#    - Set SEED_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD
#    - Set SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD
#    - Set SESSION_SECRET (generate secure random)
#    - Set CSRF_SECRET (generate secure random)
#    - Set STRIPE keys (production keys!)
#    - Set PAYPAL credentials
#    - Set SMTP credentials
#    - Set any other required variables
# 4. Save variables and cPanel restarts the app
# 5. SSH: npm run seed (creates initial admin users)
# 6. Visit https://your-domain.com to verify
#
# GENERATE SECURE SECRETS:
# $ node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# CHANGE PASSWORDS AFTER FIRST LOGIN:
# Admin Panel > Settings > Users > Change Password
# DO NOT use SEED_* passwords in production permanently!
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── TawkChat Integration (Optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Get from: https://www.tawk.to/dashboard
# Property ID: Found in Settings > Channels > Chat > Embed Code
# Widget ID: Found in Settings > Channels > Chat > Embed Code (second part)
NEXT_PUBLIC_TAWK_PROPERTY_ID=6a1ba828a3242d1c2ed9db1d
NEXT_PUBLIC_TAWK_WIDGET_ID=1jpu0ho3p

# ─── Admin JWT Secret ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secret for signing admin JWT tokens
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# IMPORTANT: Change this in production!
ADMIN_JWT_SECRET=admin-jwt-secret-change-in-production
